{"id":"4ebead6fd8a38350a179a732aa1f702feef6f774","axis":"silent","repo":"ianstormtaylor/slate","sha":"4ebead6fd8a38350a179a732aa1f702feef6f774","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".gitignore","lines":["@@ -21,3 +21,5 @@ coverage"," !/.yarn/sdks/**/lib/"," !.yarn/versions"," .pnp.*","+playwright/devices/macos/.build","+playwright/devices/android/ime/.build"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"playwright/devices/README.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@","+# Device and IME checks","+","+These scripts drive the real input layer, where synthetic Playwright key events don't reach: OS input methods on macOS, and soft keyboards on Android. Each scenario opens an example, sends input through the OS, and compares the DOM, the Slate model and the selection after each step.","+","+## macOS input methods","+","+`macos/run.cjs` opens headed Chromium and Firefox and types through real macOS input sources (Pinyin, Japanese, Korean, Russian, dead keys) with `macos/ime-key.swift`. The OS input method does the composing.","+","+Setup:","+","+1. Give your terminal Accessibility access (System Settings > Privacy & Security > Accessibility). `ime-key trusted` prints `true` when it's set.","+2. Start the examples: `yarn serve`.","+","+Run:","+","+```","+yarn node playwright/devices/macos/run.cjs [--browsers chromium,firefox] [scenario-or-issue ...]","+```","+","+While it runs, the browser takes keyboard and mouse focus. Every key checks that the test browser is the frontmost app first, so switching to another app stops the run instead of typing into it. The original input source is restored afterwards.","+","+Output is one line per scenario and browser: `PASS`, `FAIL` with the problems found, or `SKIP` when the input method didn't start composing after three tries. The `control-*` scenarios type into a plain textarea to confirm the input method works before blaming Slate.","+","+Playwright's WebKit build runs as a background app that macOS won't give keyboard focus, so input methods can't reach it. Safari coverage needs real Safari instead.","+","+## Android soft keyboards","+","+`android/run.cjs` drives Chrome on an Android emulator or a USB-connected phone. Input goes through `android/ime`, a small test keyboard app that makes the same Android input calls a keyboard like Gboard makes: set composing text, commit text, delete around the cursor, set the composing region, and key events. Chrome turns those into the same composition and `beforeinput` events a real keyboard produces.","+","+Setup:","+","+1. An emulator with Chrome (a Google Play system image) or a phone with USB debugging on. `adb devices` should list it.","+2. Start the examples: `yarn serve`.","+","+Run:","+","+```","+yarn node playwright/devices/android/run.cjs [--serial emulator-5554] [scenario-or-issue ...]","+```","+","+The script builds and installs the test keyboard on first use (needs the Android SDK build tools and a JDK), selects it, opens the example through `adb reverse`, and connects Playwright to Chrome's DevTools socket. It selects Gboard again when it finishes; set `KEEP_TEST_IME=1` to leave the test keyboard on.","+","+The test keyboard sends the calls a scenario lists. Real keyboards differ in which calls they make and in what order, so a passing scenario shows Slate handles that sequence, not that every keyboard works.","+","+Use separate emulator, example-server and DevTools ports for concurrent runs:","+","+```sh","+SLATE_PORT=3200 DEVTOOLS_PORT=9335 yarn node playwright/devices/android/run.cjs --serial emulator-5556 item35-second-composing-character-new-line","+```","+","+The `item35-*` scenarios add touch selection, suggestion replacement, sending during composition, paragraph formatting and scroll-container checks. Letter/digit, text/void, composing/committed and keyboard/touch controls distinguish input setup failures from the reported editing behavior. The image-tap cases substitute a local SVG for the example's remote image requests so they do not depend on the image host.","+","+`tap` sends an Android `adb input tap` by default and checks that a trusted touch reached the requested element, then waits for its click before the scenario continues. It reads Chrome’s `toolbar_hairline` bounds from `uiautomator`, then chooses a visible, hit-tested client rectangle and converts it using the current visual viewport and device scale. Set `CDP_TAPS=1` to use Chrome DevTools touch dispatch for scenario taps instead. The initial editor tap remains native so Android establishes the keyboard input connection. Text still goes through Android InputConnection. `keyboardShown` reads Android's `mInputShown` state. `hideKeyboard` sends Android's Back key to establish a hidden-keyboard precondition before comparing text and mention taps. `composeSequence` sends composing prefixes without the usual per-step pause; adb transport still adds latency, so this does not model every fast physical keyboard.","+","+Firefox for Android can be driven by geckodriver using `moz:firefoxOptions.androidPackage` and `androidDeviceSerial`. Complete its first-run screens and open a web page before waiting for a WebDriver session; the native home screen does not create a Marionette content window. WebDriver touch actions alone did not establish a test-keyboard input connection in the probe, while an adb touchscreen tap did. The Chrome runner is not a Firefox runner; verify both model and DOM when probing Firefox separately.","+","+The Gboard probes use the keyboard’s accessibility key bounds from a fresh `uiautomator dump --windows`; they do not assume a screen size or fixed key coordinates. They require an English Gboard layout with the requested key labels exposed. A missing key stops the probe rather than guessing its location.","+","+```sh","+ANDROID_SERIAL=emulator-5556 SLATE_PORT=3200 DEVTOOLS_PORT=9335 yarn node playwright/devices/gboard-6022.cjs","+ANDROID_SERIAL=emulator-5556 SLATE_PORT=3200 DEVTOOLS_PORT=9335 yarn node playwright/devices/gboard-5099.cjs","+```","+","+The first probe toggles bold and types `bold`; the second clears the editor, presses Backspace three times, then types `asd`. Both keep the original model/keyboard diagnostics. Reading a fresh key dump adds time between Gboard keystrokes, so these probes establish the recorded sequence rather than rapid typing behavior.","+","+The touch geometry check runs without a device:","+","+```sh","+yarn node --test playwright/devices/android/touch.test.cjs","+```","+","+`item37-tap-mention-composing` records the native failure after composing `pending`, selecting a mention, pressing Backspace and composing `after`. The finished-composition and visible-keyboard controls exercise the same selection and deletion without an active composition. These are device regressions, so the composing case is expected to fail until the library handles the missing composition end. No synthetic composition event is used in the regression."],"additions":72,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"playwright/devices/android/ime/AndroidManifest.xml","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@","+<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"utf-8\"?>","+<manifest xmlns:android=\"http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android\" package=\"org.slatejs.testime\">","+  <uses-sdk android:minSdkVersion=\"26\" android:targetSdkVersion=\"35\" />","+  <application android:label=\"Slate Test IME\">","+    <service","+      android:name=\".TestIme\"","+      android:label=\"Slate Test IME\"","+      android:permission=\"android.permission.BIND_INPUT_METHOD\"","+      android:exported=\"true\">","+      <intent-filter>","+        <action android:name=\"android.view.InputMethod\" />","+      </intent-filter>","+      <meta-data android:name=\"android.view.im\" android:resource=\"@xml/method\" />","+    </service>","+  </application>","+</manifest>"],"additions":16,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"playwright/devices/android/ime/build.sh","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@","+#!/bin/sh","+set -e","+SDK=\"${ANDROID_HOME:-$HOME/Library/Android/sdk}\"","+TOOLS=\"$SDK/build-tools/$(ls \"$SDK/build-tools\" | sort -V | tail -1)\"","+PLATFORM=\"$SDK/platforms/$(ls \"$SDK/platforms\" | sort -V | tail -1)/android.jar\"","+HERE=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"","+OUT=\"${1:-$HERE/.build}\"","+rm -rf \"$OUT\" && mkdir -p \"$OUT/classes\" \"$OUT/res\"","+\"$TOOLS/aapt2\" compile --dir \"$HERE/res\" -o \"$OUT/res.zip\"","+\"$TOOLS/aapt2\" link -I \"$PLATFORM\" --manifest \"$HERE/AndroidManifest.xml\" -o \"$OUT/unsigned.apk\" \"$OUT/res.zip\"","+javac -source 11 -target 11 -nowarn -classpath \"$PLATFORM\" -d \"$OUT/classes\" $(find \"$HERE/src\" -name '*.java')","+\"$TOOLS/d8\" --lib \"$PLATFORM\" --min-api 26 --output \"$OUT\" $(find \"$OUT/classes\" -name '*.class')","+(cd \"$OUT\" && zip -q unsigned.apk classes.dex)","+\"$TOOLS/zipalign\" -f 4 \"$OUT/unsigned.apk\" \"$OUT/aligned.apk\"","+KEYSTORE=\"$OUT/debug.keystore\"","+keytool -genkeypair -keystore \"$KEYSTORE\" -storepass android -keypass android -alias slate -keyalg RSA -validity 10000 -dname \"CN=Slate Test\" >/dev/null 2>&1","+\"$TOOLS/apksigner\" sign --ks \"$KEYSTORE\" --ks-pass pass:android --out \"$OUT/slate-test-ime.apk\" \"$OUT/aligned.apk\"","+echo \"$OUT/slate-test-ime.apk\""],"additions":18,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"playwright/devices/android/ime/res/xml/method.xml","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@","+<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"utf-8\"?>","+<input-method xmlns:android=\"http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android\" />"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"playwright/devices/android/ime/src/org/slatejs/testime/TestIme.java","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,104 @@","+package org.slatejs.testime;","+","+import android.content.BroadcastReceiver;","+import android.content.Context;","+import android.content.Intent;","+import android.content.IntentFilter;","+import android.inputmethodservice.InputMethodService;","+import android.util.Base64;","+import android.view.View;","+import android.view.inputmethod.ExtractedText;","+import android.view.inputmethod.ExtractedTextRequest;","+import android.view.inputmethod.InputConnection;","+import android.widget.TextView;","+import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;","+","+public class TestIme extends InputMethodService {","+  static final String ACTION = \"org.slatejs.testime.COMMAND\";","+","+  private final BroadcastReceiver receiver =","+      new BroadcastReceiver() {","+        @Override","+        public void onReceive(Context context, Intent intent) {","+          setResultData(run(intent));","+        }","+      };","+","+  @Override","+  public void onCreate() {","+    super.onCreate();","+    registerReceiver(receiver, new IntentFilter(ACTION), Context.RECEIVER_EXPORTED);","+  }","+","+  @Override","+  public void onDestroy() {","+    unregisterReceiver(receiver);","+    super.onDestroy();","+  }","+","+  @Override","+  public View onCreateInputView() {","+    TextView view = new TextView(this);","+    view.setText(\"Slate test keyboard\");","+    view.setMinHeight(240);","+    return view;","+  }","+","+  @Override","+  public boolean onEvaluateFullscreenMode() {","+    return false;","+  }","+","+  private String decodedText(Intent intent) {","+    String encoded = intent.getStringExtra(\"b64\");","+    if (encoded == null) return \"\";","+    return new String(Base64.decode(encoded, Base64.DEFAULT), StandardCharsets.UTF_8);","+  }","+","+  private String run(Intent intent) {","+    InputConnection connection = getCurrentInputConnection();","+    if (connection == null) return \"error:no-input-connection\";","+    String op = intent.getStringExtra(\"op\");","+    String text = decodedText(intent);","+    int a = intent.getIntExtra(\"a\", 1);","+    int b = intent.getIntExtra(\"b\", 0);","+    boolean ok;","+    switch (op == null ? \"\" : op) {","+      case \"compose\":","+        ok = connection.setComposingText(text, 1);","+        break;","+      case \"commit\":","+        ok = connection.commitText(text, 1);","+        break;","+      case \"finish\":","+        ok = connection.finishComposingText();","+        break;","+      case \"delete\":","+        ok = connection.deleteSurroundingText(a, b);","+        break;","+      case \"region\":","+        ok = connection.setComposingRegion(a, b);","+        break;","+      case \"select\":","+        ok = connection.setSelection(a, b);","+        break;","+      case \"key\":","+        sendDownUpKeyEvents(a);","+        ok = true;","+        break;","+      case \"begin\":","+        ok = connection.beginBatchEdit();","+        break;","+      case \"end\":","+        ok = connection.endBatchEdit();","+        break;","+      case \"state\":","+        ExtractedText extracted = connection.getExtractedText(new ExtractedTextRequest(), 0);","+        if (extracted == null) return \"state:none\";","+        return \"state:\" + extracted.selectionStart + \":\" + extracted.selectionEnd + \":\" + extracted.text;","+      default:","+        return \"error:unknown-op:\" + op;","+    }","+    return ok ? \"ok\" : \"error:rejected\";","+  }","+}"],"additions":104,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"playwright/devices/android/run.cjs","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,289 @@","+const { execFileSync } = require('child_process')","+const path = require('path')","+const { chromium } = require('@playwright/test')","+const {","+  consistencyProblems,","+  installRecorder,","+  placeCaret,","+  readState,","+  waitForEditor,","+  withEditor,","+} = require('../runner.cjs')","+const scenarios = require('../scenarios/android.cjs')","+const { tapLocator } = require('./touch.cjs')","+","+const SDK =","+  process.env.ANDROID_HOME || path.join(process.env.HOME, 'Library/Android/sdk')","+const ADB = process.env.ADB || path.join(SDK, 'platform-tools', 'adb')","+const PORT = Number(process.env.SLATE_PORT || 3000)","+const DEVTOOLS_PORT = Number(process.env.DEVTOOLS_PORT || 9333)","+const TEST_IME = 'org.slatejs.testime/.TestIme'","+const GBOARD =","+  'com.google.android.inputmethod.latin/com.android.inputmethod.latin.LatinIME'","+const APK = path.join(__dirname, 'ime', '.build', 'slate-test-ime.apk')","+","+const args = process.argv.slice(2)","+const option = name => {","+  const index = args.indexOf(`--${name}`)","+  return index === -1 ? null : args.splice(index, 2)[1]","+}","+const serial = option('serial') || process.env.ANDROID_SERIAL","+const only = args","+","+const adb = (...adbArgs) =>","+  execFileSync(ADB, [...(serial ? ['-s', serial] : []), ...adbArgs], {","+    encoding: 'utf8',","+  }).trim()","+","+const keyCodes = {","+  enter: 66,","+  delete: 67,","+  forwardDelete: 112,","+  left: 21,","+  right: 22,","+}","+","+const imeCommand = (op, { text, a, b } = {}) => {","+  const commandArgs = [","+    'shell',","+    'am',","+    'broadcast',","+    '-a',","+    'org.slatejs.testime.COMMAND',","+    '--es',","+    'op',","+    op,","+  ]","+  if (text != null) {","+    commandArgs.push(","+      '--es',","+      'b64',","+      Buffer.from(text, 'utf8').toString('base64')","+    )","+  }","+  if (a != null) commandArgs.push('--ei', 'a', String(a))","+  if (b != null) commandArgs.push('--ei', 'b', String(b))","+  const output = adb(...commandArgs)","+  const result = /data=\"([^\"]*)\"/.exec(output)?.[1]","+  if (!result || result.startsWith('error')) {","+    throw new Error(`test keyboard ${op} failed: ${result || output}`)","+  }","+  return result","+}","+","+const setUp = () => {","+  if (","+    !adb('shell', 'pm', 'list', 'packages', 'org.slatejs.testime').includes(","+      'testime'","+    )","+  ) {","+    execFileSync(path.join(__dirname, 'ime', 'build.sh'), { stdio: 'ignore' })","+    adb('install', '-r', APK)","+  }","+  adb('shell', 'ime', 'enable', TEST_IME)","+  adb('shell', 'ime', 'set', TEST_IME)","+  adb('reverse', `tcp:${PORT}`, `tcp:${PORT}`)","+  adb('shell', 'am', 'set-debug-app', '--persistent', 'com.android.chrome')","+  adb(","+    'shell',","+    'echo \"_ --disable-fre --no-default-browser-check --no-first-run\" > /data/local/tmp/chrome-command-line'","+  )","+  if (","+    !adb('shell', 'cat', '/proc/net/unix').includes('chrome_devtools_remote')","+  ) {","+    adb(","+      'shell',","+      'am',","+      'start',","+      '-a',","+      'android.intent.action.VIEW',","+      '-d',","+      `http://localhost:${PORT}/`,","+      'com.android.chrome'","+    )","+    for (let attempt = 0; attempt < 30; attempt++) {","+      if (","+        adb('shell', 'cat', '/proc/net/unix').includes('chrome_devtools_remote')","+      )","+        break","+      execFileSync('sleep', ['1'])","+    }","+  }","+  adb('forward', `tcp:${DEVTOOLS_PORT}`, 'localabstract:chrome_devtools_remote')","+}","+","+const recordedPages = new WeakSet()","+","+const openExample = async (browser, example, localImages) => {","+  const url = `http://localhost:${PORT}/examples/${example}`","+  let page = browser.contexts()[0]?.pages()[0]","+  if (!page) {","+    adb(","+      'shell',","+      'am',","+      'start',","+      '-a',","+      'android.intent.action.VIEW',","+      '-d',","+      url,","+      'com.android.chrome'","+    )","+    await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 3000))","+    page = browser.contexts()[0].pages()[0]","+  }","+  if (!recordedPages.has(page)) {","+    recordedPages.add(page)","+    await installRecorder(page)","+  }","+  if (localImages) {","+    await page.route('https://source.unsplash.com/**', route =>","+      route.fulfill({","+        contentType: 'image/svg+xml',","+        body: '<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\"><rect width=\"320\" height=\"180\" fill=\"teal\"/></svg>',","+      })","+    )","+  }","+  await page.bringToFront()","+  await page.goto(url)","+  await page.locator('[data-slate-editor]').waitFor()","+  await waitForEditor(page)","+  return page","+}","+","+const runScenario = async (browser, scenario) => {","+  const page = await openExample(","+    browser,","+    scenario.example,","+    scenario.localImages","+  )","+  const errors = []","+  const onError = error => errors.push(error.message)","+  const onConsole = message => {","+    if (message.type() === 'error' && !message.text().startsWith('Warning:'))","+      errors.push(message.text())","+  }","+  page.on('pageerror', onError)","+  page.on('console', onConsole)","+  const settle = () => page.waitForTimeout(250)","+  const ctx = {","+    page,","+    tap: async locator => {","+      await tapLocator(page, locator, adb, process.env.CDP_TAPS === '1')","+      await settle()","+    },","+    hideKeyboard: async () => {","+      adb('shell', 'input', 'keyevent', '4')","+      await page.waitForTimeout(800)","+    },","+    keyboardShown: () => {","+      const state = adb('shell', 'dumpsys', 'input_method')","+      const match = /mInputShown=(true|false)/.exec(state)","+      if (!match) throw new Error('keyboard visibility missing from dumpsys')","+      return match[1] === 'true'","+    },","+    composeSequence: async values => {","+      for (const text of values) imeCommand('compose', { text })","+      await settle()","+    },","+    compose: async text => (imeCommand('compose', { text }), settle()),","+    commit: async text => (imeCommand('commit', { text }), settle()),","+    finish: async () => (imeCommand('finish'), settle()),","+    deleteAround: async (before, after = 0) => (","+      imeCommand('delete', { a: before, b: after }), settle()","+    ),","+    region: async (start, end) => (","+      imeCommand('region', { a: start, b: end }), settle()","+    ),","+    setSelection: async (start, end = start) => (","+      imeCommand('select', { a: start, b: end }), settle()","+    ),","+    key: async (name, count = 1) => {","+      for (let index = 0; index < count; index++) {","+        imeCommand('key', { a: keyCodes[name] ?? name })","+        await settle()","+      }","+    },","+    imeState: () => imeCommand('state'),","+    typeWord: async word => {","+      for (let length = 1; length <= word.length; length++) {","+        imeCommand('compose', { text: word.slice(0, length) })","+        await page.waitForTimeout(60)","+      }","+      await settle()","+    },","+    caret: where => placeCaret(page, where),","+    editor: (fn, value) => withEditor(page, fn, value),","+    wait: ms => page.waitForTimeout(ms),","+    state: () => readState(page),","+  }","+  let problems = []","+  try {","+    await tapLocator(","+      page,","+      page.locator('[data-slate-editor] [data-slate-string]').first(),","+      adb","+    )","+    await settle()","+    imeCommand('state')","+    problems = (await scenario.run(ctx)) || []","+    await page.waitForTimeout(400)","+  } catch (error) {","+    problems.push(`step failed: ${error.message.split('\\n')[0]}`)","+  }","+  let state","+  try {","+    state = await readState(page)","+  } catch (error) {","+    problems.push(","+      `editor unreadable at ${page.url()}: ${error.message.split('\\n')[0]}`","+    )","+    state = { model: [], events: [] }","+  }","+  if (state.dom && !scenario.allowInconsistentDom)","+    problems.push(...consistencyProblems(state))","+  problems.push(...errors.map(error => `page error: ${error}`))","+  page.off('pageerror', onError)","+  page.off('console', onConsole)","+  return { problems, state }","+}","+","+;(async () => {","+  setUp()","+  const browser = await chromium.connectOverCDP(","+    `http://localhost:${DEVTOOLS_PORT}`","+  )","+  const selected = scenarios.filter(","+    scenario =>","+      only.length === 0 ||","+      only.includes(scenario.name) ||","+      scenario.issues.some(issue => only.includes(String(issue)))","+  )","+  const results = []","+  for (const scenario of selected) {","+    const { problems, state } = await runScenario(browser, scenario)","+    const passed = problems.length === 0","+    results.push({ scenario: scenario.name, passed, problems })","+    process.stdout.write(","+      `${passed ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'} android ${scenario.name} (${scenario.issues","+        .map(issue => `#${issue}`)","+        .join(' ')})\\n`","+    )","+    for (const problem of problems) process.stdout.write(`  ${problem}\\n`)","+    if (!passed || process.env.VERBOSE) {","+      process.stdout.write(`  model ${JSON.stringify(state.model)}\\n`)","+      process.stdout.write(`  events ${state.events.slice(-30).join(' ')}\\n`)","+    }","+  }","+  await browser.close()","+  if (process.env.KEEP_TEST_IME !== '1') adb('shell', 'ime', 'set', GBOARD)","+  if (process.env.RESULTS) {","+    require('fs').writeFileSync(","+      process.env.RESULTS,","+      JSON.stringify(results, null, 2)","+    )","+  }","+  process.exit(results.every(result => result.passed) ? 0 : 1)","+})().catch(error => {","+  process.stderr.write(`${error.stack}\\n`)","+  process.exit(1)","+})"],"additions":289,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"playwright/devices/android/touch.cjs","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,130 @@","+const readUi = adb => {","+  const output = adb(","+    'shell',","+    'uiautomator',","+    'dump',","+    '--windows',","+    '/sdcard/slate-device-ui.xml'","+  )","+  if (!output.includes('UI hierchary dumped to:'))","+    throw new Error('Android UI dump did not complete')","+  const xml = adb('exec-out', 'cat', '/sdcard/slate-device-ui.xml')","+  return Array.from(xml.matchAll(/<node\\s([^>]+)>/g), match => {","+    const node = Object.fromEntries(","+      Array.from(match[1].matchAll(/([\\w-]+)=\"([^\"]*)\"/g), ([, key, value]) => [","+        key,","+        value,","+      ])","+    )","+    const bounds = /\\[(-?\\d+),(-?\\d+)\\]\\[(-?\\d+),(-?\\d+)\\]/.exec(node.bounds)","+    if (bounds) node.rect = bounds.slice(1).map(Number)","+    return node","+  })","+}","+","+const tapKey = (adb, key) => {","+  const node = readUi(adb).find(","+    node =>","+      node.package === 'com.google.android.inputmethod.latin' &&","+      node['content-desc'].toLowerCase() === key.toLowerCase() &&","+      node.rect &&","+      node.rect[2] > node.rect[0] &&","+      node.rect[3] > node.rect[1]","+  )","+  if (!node)","+    throw new Error(","+      `Gboard key ${JSON.stringify(key)} is not visible in the UI dump`","+    )","+  const [left, top, right, bottom] = node.rect","+  adb(","+    'shell',","+    'input',","+    'tap',","+    String(Math.round((left + right) / 2)),","+    String(Math.round((top + bottom) / 2))","+  )","+}","+","+const tapLocator = async (page, locator, adb, cdp = false) => {","+  await locator.scrollIntoViewIfNeeded()","+  const toolbar =","+    !cdp &&","+    readUi(adb).find(","+      node => node['resource-id'] === 'com.android.chrome:id/toolbar_hairline'","+    )","+  if (!cdp && !toolbar?.rect) throw new Error('Chrome toolbar bounds missing')","+  const point = await locator.evaluate(element => {","+    const viewport = visualViewport","+    for (const rect of element.getClientRects()) {","+      const left = Math.max(rect.left, viewport.offsetLeft)","+      const right = Math.min(rect.right, viewport.offsetLeft + viewport.width)","+      const top = Math.max(rect.top, viewport.offsetTop)","+      const bottom = Math.min(rect.bottom, viewport.offsetTop + viewport.height)","+      if (right <= left || bottom <= top) continue","+      const x = (left + right) / 2","+      const y = (top + bottom) / 2","+      if (!element.contains(document.elementFromPoint(x, y))) continue","+      return {","+        x: x - viewport.offsetLeft,","+        y: y - viewport.offsetTop,","+        scale: devicePixelRatio * viewport.scale,","+      }","+    }","+    throw new Error('tap target has no visible hit-testable rectangle')","+  })","+  await locator.evaluate(element => {","+    window.__slateDeviceTap = null","+    window.__slateDeviceClick = false","+    element.addEventListener(","+      'click',","+      () => {","+        window.__slateDeviceClick = true","+      },","+      { once: true, capture: true }","+    )","+    element.addEventListener(","+      '